# Portability patches for the Wave upstream (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).

patch: wave-1ul-vf2
why: The upstream builds 64-bit masks with `1UL << n` on 64-bit words (wave_word is uint64_t).
why: `unsigned long` is 64 bits only on LP64 systems; on Windows (LLP64) and wasm32 it is 32
why: bits, so for n >= 32 the shift is undefined and the masks are wrong. Keygen then fails its
why: Gaussian elimination and writes past a buffer (clang-cl ASan: heap-buffer-overflow in
why: vf3_set_coeff, CI run 45270462977). `1ULL` is at least 64 bits everywhere and gives the
why: same value as `1UL` on LP64 systems, so Linux and macOS results do not change.
file: upstream/Wave822/fq_arithmetic/vf2.c
count: 1
find: 1UL <<
replace: 1ULL <<

